{
  // THIS FILE SHOULD BE EMPTY, AND ONE ENTRY BELOW IS THE ONLY EXCEPTION LEFT.
  //
  // Every task a project needs is defined ONCE in `alex-projects.code-workspace`,
  // routed through devkit's `devkit_project.py`, and takes the checkout as a picker.
  // Testing, linting, the vendored-harness hook tests, the drift check, the
  // agent-context sync, the git sync, starting and stopping this project's Docker
  // stack, Docker daemon recovery, ports, and every shipping step already exist there.
  // None of them belong here.
  //
  // A TASK IN THIS FILE IS DUPLICATED PER WORKTREE, and that is the whole argument.
  // The workspace holds a checkout plus an ephemeral box per agent task in flight — so
  // a task defined here is rendered once per live worktree in the quick-pick, under one
  // label, with nothing to say which checkout it would run in. The copies then
  // disagree the moment the worktrees sit on different branches. That is not a
  // hypothetical: back when every project also carried a static `-b` sibling,
  // carameli's two copies had drifted to eight tasks versus two, and ibkr_trader's to
  // five versus eleven, with the same label ("Stop: Docker Stack") running different
  // commands in each.
  //
  // A PROJECT-SPECIFIC TASK IS STILL HOISTED. It does not have to become generic to go
  // up: `devkit_project.py`'s `Action.projects` scopes an action to one repo's worktree
  // pair, and the workspace gives it a two-option picker. carameli's Playwright run and
  // ibkr_trader's IBKR backtests live up there that way. So "it is only useful in this
  // one repo" is NOT a reason to define a task here — it is the case the scoping exists
  // for. This template shipped five tasks once; four went, then sixteen more across the
  // live checkouts, then the last two files entirely.
  //
  // THIS FILE IS NOW EMPTY, INCLUDING FOR ALEMBIC PROJECTS. "DB: New Migration" was the
  // last holdout; it went up once carameli and ibkr_trader each grew a
  // `scripts/db-revision.py` contract entrypoint, and it is scoped to `DB_PROJECTS` so
  // `--check` never demands that script from devkit or a `bare` preset.
  //
  // ONE CONSEQUENCE TO KNOW ABOUT: a project generated from this template does not get
  // the migration task until someone adds it to `DB_PROJECTS` and the `dbCheckout`
  // picker, because those live in devkit's source and the workspace file, neither of
  // which `new-project.py` can extend the way it extends the `folders` list and the
  // `project` picker. Until then, `alembic revision --autogenerate -m "..."` is the
  // documented interface, which is what it was before this task ever existed. Do NOT
  // "fix" that by putting the task back here — it would be duplicated per worktree the
  // moment an agent box is cut against the project, which is the whole problem.
  //
  // What this project owes the arrangement instead is the CLI CONTRACT: keep
  // `scripts/run-tests.py`, `scripts/lint-all.py`, `scripts/docker-up.py`,
  // `scripts/docker-down.py`, `scripts/sync-codex-context.py` and
  // `scripts/sync-devkit.py` at those paths, accepting their usual arguments.
  // `devkit_project.py --check` reports any checkout that has stopped satisfying it.
  // The scripts stay per-project on purpose — lint scope, test scope and compose
  // topology genuinely differ — which is why they live in `templates/` and not in
  // `sync-devkit.py`'s MANIFEST.
  //
  // Conventions, wherever a task ends up living: label `"Domain: Title Case Action"`;
  // every task carries a `detail` (the second line of the quick-pick, and the only
  // place a one-click action can state its cost or blast radius); every task carries an
  // `icon` with an id and colour no other task uses, so a long list stays scannable;
  // `"type": "process"` so VS Code monitors the process directly and the exit-code icon
  // stays truthful; `notify-wrap.py` for the completion toast; and every
  // `${input:...}` picker supplies one real token in every branch, because an empty
  // string reaches argparse as a stray positional and is rejected.
  "version": "2.0.0",
  "tasks": [],
  "inputs": []
}
